function infoCa_injectToCodex()
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addCategory', 'ca_cat', 'Cosmic Ascendancy'%_t, 'data/textures/icons/vortex.png')

    -- The Eclipse Crisis (Deep Dive)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c0', 'The Eclipse Crisis (Deep Dive)'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a0', 'Eclipse Faction Stats & Traits'%_t, 'Eclipse vessels are exceptionally deadly due to their specialized "Void Shields" and highly coordinated AI logic:\n- Void Shields: Incoming physical damage (Cannons, Bolters, Chainguns) is mitigated by 80%. You must use high-tier Energy/Antimatter/Plasma weapons to strip their shields.\n- Armor Plating: Base Hull HP is multiplied by 2.5x relative to vanilla generated ships of the same volume. Furthermore, all Eclipse blueprints have been upgraded to use Avorion (Tier 6) material blocks, granting them colossal base health pools.\n- Weaponry: The Eclipse exclusively utilize massive EMP lasers and high-velocity Plasma Artillery, making them incredibly lethal against your own shields.\n- Aesthetics & Classes: Eclipse ships are towering, jet-black monolithic structures accented by crimson energy fields. They fly Nullifiers (Pyramids), Obliterators (Monoliths), Harbingers (Obelisks), and 4 specialized combat classes: the Juggernaut (Dreadnought), Interceptor (Fighter), Harvester (Miner), and Defiler (Assault Frigate).\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a_abilities', 'Eclipse Combat Abilities'%_t, 'Eclipse ships wield devastating, class-specific mechanics to obliterate fleets:\n- Dark Matter Blink (All Ships): Upon taking 15% burst damage within 1 second, the ship will violently blink 5-10km away to escape, leaving behind a Void Rift (cooldown: 45s).\n- Ethereal Phase-Shift (Interceptors & Phantoms): Slippery vanguards instantly phase out of reality for 4 seconds upon shield break, becoming an invincible void-shadow to reposition and healing 25% of their shields.\n- Adaptive Resistance (Defilers & Artillery): These heavy combatants analyze incoming fire; taking 5% Hull/Shield damage from a specific element (e.g., Plasma) triggers a 15-second resistance to that element where they heal back 50% of the incoming damage!\n- Void Siphon Aura (Command Ships): Massive command ships constantly project a 10km devouring aura, rapidly draining the shield capacity of all nearby player ships to heal themselves for 25% of the drained amount.\n- Singularity Implosion (Capital Ships): Upon death, these gargantuan reactors collapse. After a 3-second warning, they violently detonate, stripping 15% of a player\'s Max Hull within 3km!\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a1', 'Invasion Mechanics & Threat Escalation'%_t, 'The Eclipse dynamically targets sectors containing high player or AI faction value.\n- Scouting Phase: Small, fast-moving Eclipse Interceptors will arrive in a sector. If they are not destroyed within 5 minutes, they broadcast a beacon.\n- Assault Phase: Once the beacon is active, a massive invasion fleet will warp in.\n  - Fleet Composition: 1 Dreadnought, 3 Cruisers, 5-8 Corvettes.\n- Eradication: Eclipse fleets prioritize destroying Stations. If they destroy an AI faction station, the sector\'s local economic output drops permanently. If they destroy a Player station, the player obviously loses that asset.\n- Personal Ambushes: The Eclipse actively hunts players. Every 25-45 minutes, there is a 40% chance that an elite Eclipse strike team will personally ambush the player\'s current sector.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a2', 'Eclipse Citadels'%_t, 'When an invasion is overwhelmingly successful, the Eclipse will permanently occupy the sector and construct a Citadel.\n- The Lockdown Matrix: Citadels generate a sector-wide interdiction field. Ships cannot jump out of a Citadel sector unless the Citadel is destroyed.\n- Siege Mechanics: Citadels have 200,000,000 base HP (scaling with difficulty) and are surrounded by 4 orbital defense platforms. \n- Loot: Destroying a Citadel guarantees a drop of 1-3 Legendary subsystems and massive quantities of Avorion ore, alongside unique crafting materials for the Ascendancy Forge.\n- Suppression Field: Destroying a Citadel halts all Eclipse invasions within a 15-sector radius for exactly 6 real-time hours.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a7', 'The Dark Sector'%_t, 'Deep within the Galactic Core (Barrier), players may encounter Eclipse-controlled Dark Sectors.\n- Spawn: When jumping into completely un-generated space inside the core, there is a 20% risk of it transforming into a Dark Sector.\n- Hazard: The sector is engulfed in dense Dark Matter Fog and dominated by Eclipse Citadels guarded by Juggernaut dreadnoughts.\n- Reward: These sectors contain extremely dense Ascendant Matter and Ogonite asteroid fields, making them incredibly lucrative if you survive.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a6', 'The World Eater (Endgame Boss)'%_t, 'The World Eater is a 6-kilometer long Pyramid dreadnought built entirely of Avorion that spawns every 3-5 hours.\n\n- Invulnerability Tethers: At 50% and 25% Hull, it spawns Anchor Pylons and becomes immune to damage until they are destroyed.\n- Quantum EMP Hazard: Periodically targets a player with a massive cyan glow. After 3 seconds, an EMP erupts, instantly stripping 100% of their shields and inflicting 25% Max Hull damage.\n- Gravity Anomaly Hazard: Spawns a dark purple Black Hole that pulls ships in and inflicts 5% Max Hull damage per second!\n- World-Breaker Laser: An axial beam that locks the boss in place and fires a blast dealing 100% of Max Shields + 50% of Max Hull.\n- Emergency Repairs: At 50% HP, the World-Eater initiates emergency repairs, violently blinking away and healing 5% of its colossal Max Hull.\n- Enrage Phase: At 35% HP, unleashes a second global EMP and enters an Enraged state (+50% Fire Rate, +50% Global Damage, projects a Dark Matter Aura).\n- Raid Summoning: Jettisoning an Eclipse Datacore from your cargo hold tears open a hyperspace rift and instantly summons the World-Eater to your location!\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a9', 'The Fallen Empire Awakening'%_t, 'The Eclipse evolves after conquering 10 sectors (or 75 in legacy configs).\n- Crusaders: The Eclipse deploy ultra-heavy Crusade fleets to systematically hunt down and wipe out AI Faction Capitals.\n- Dark Matter Fog: Sectors captured by the Eclipse become veiled in Dark Matter Fog, imposing harsh debuffs to sensors and jump drives.\n- Weather Immunity: Awakened Eclipse ships are immune to all hazard weather effects.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c0', 'ca_cat_a10', 'Defeating Nemeses & Damage Gates'%_t, 'Elite Eclipse combatants, known as Nemeses, employ extreme survivability tactics:\n- Damage Gates: Nemesis shields and hulls cannot take more than 8% of their maximum health as damage per tick, preventing one-shot mechanics.\n- Elemental Resistances: Nemeses can dynamically adapt their hull plating to resist specific damage types that they have recently received.\n'%_t, '')

    -- The Ascendant Campaign
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c4', 'The Ascendant Campaign'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c4', 'ca_cat_a14', 'Aegis, The Ascendant Envoy'%_t, 'Upon defeating the Wormhole Guardian and unleashing The Eclipse, you will be physically intercepted by Aegis, an ancient AI construct designed by the creators of the dimensional prison.\n\n- Physical Rendezvous: Instead of receiving basic radio messages, Aegis will transmit secure rendezvous coordinates to you. You must physically fly to these sectors to meet her projection.\n- 5-Part Storyline: She will guide you through a fully-scripted 5-mission campaign detailing the origins of The Eclipse, the location of the Ascendancy Forge, and the incoming World-Eater.\n- Massive Rewards: Returning to Aegis for a debrief injects massive credit payouts (scaling up to 25 Million) and high-tier equipment drops directly into your cargo hold.\n- Multiplayer Support: If you are playing with an alliance, Aegis will patiently remain stationed at the rendezvous point until all players in the sector have had a chance to speak with her and claim their own personal rewards!\n'%_t, '')

    -- The Ascendancy Beacon
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c1', 'The Ascendancy Beacon'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c1', 'ca_cat_a3', 'Ascendancy Beacon Functionality'%_t, 'Players can construct the ultimate megastructure: The Ascendancy Beacon.\n\n- Permanent Sector Simulation: A sector containing an active Ascendancy Beacon is simulated 24/7, even if no players are online.\n- Global Buffs: The beacon applies a permanent, massive stat multiplier to all ships in the player\'s fleet across the entire galaxy.\n- Upgrades: The beacon can be upgraded through 5 tiers, exponentially increasing the global stat buffs but requiring massive, continuous upkeep costs of Credits, Avorion, and Ogonite.\n- The Grand Toll & Treasury Payouts: The beacon acts as an intergalactic border checkpoint. All NPC traders and AI factions jumping into the sector are charged a massive entry tax. The Beacon safely stores all collected tolls in its internal treasury and pays out a single lump-sum to your faction every 45 minutes.\n- Dynamic Wartime Premium: AI factions currently engaged in massive wars (Cosmic War integration) will desperately pay up to a +50% Premium Toll for seeking safe harbor in your heavily defended capital sector!\n- Capital Sieges: A hidden playtime clock runs within the beacon. Every 3 to 6 hours, a devastating siege fleet (Pirates, Xsotan, or War Factions) will invade your sector to destroy the beacon. If you defend it, you earn legendary loot. If it falls, your global buffs collapse.\n'%_t, '')

    -- The Ascendancy Forge (Crafting & Math)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c2', 'The Ascendancy Forge (Crafting & Math)'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a4', 'Unlock Requirements'%_t, 'To combat the Eclipse, players must locate and utilize the Ascendancy Forge to craft gear that pushes past Avorion\'s native limits.\n\n- The Forge is discovered during "Forging the Defense," the second stage of the Ascendant Campaign.\n- Access is unlocked by feeding it an Eclipse Datacore via the "Decrypt Eclipse Datacore" option, salvaged from destroyed Eclipse vessels.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a5', 'Crafting Formula & Sacrifice Mechanics'%_t, 'Crafting Ascendant-tier gear is extraordinarily expensive to balance its extreme power.\n\n- Base Cost: 50,000,000 Credits, 250,000 Avorion, 150,000 Ogonite.\n- The Sacrifice System: When initiating a craft, the Forge requires a Catalyst. You must sacrifice existing Legendary or Exotic subsystems.\n  - Math: Sacrificing 1 Legendary grants a 20% success rate. Sacrificing 5 Legendaries guarantees a 100% success rate.\n  - Failure: If the craft fails, the sacrificed subsystems and half the raw materials are destroyed, but you are given "Ascendant Scrap" which slightly boosts the success rate of the next attempt.\n- The Stellar Forge: Exchange 1+ Billion Credits and massive ore reserves to asynchronously craft custom God-Tier weapons or Relic Subsystems over 24 real-time hours.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a8', 'Titan Weaponry & Cybernetics'%_t, 'The Forge is capable of synthesizing incredibly complex superweapons and biological augmentations.\n\n- Ascendant World-Breaker (Titan Coaxial): A gargantuan, dreadnought-class axial beam laser dealing 250,000 continuous damage. Firing this weapon locks the ship\'s rotation.\n- Ascendant Neural Implant: A terrifying fusion of Eclipse technology and human neuro-links. This equippable ship subsystem massively augments the ship\'s captain, scaling up fighter control, jump reach, velocity, and weapons.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a11', 'Factory Overdrive & Forge Decryption'%_t, 'Players can overclock their player-owned stations and their entire fleet through the Forge.\n\n- Factory Overdrive: By feeding 50 Ascendant Matter into the Forge, players can initiate a Factory Overdrive. All player stations will experience a 300% production speed boost for 1 real-time hour.\n- Forge Decryption Matrix: The Ascendancy Forge now accepts Eclipse Datacores. Decrypting them permanently raises your Global Ascendancy Tier, granting +15% Shields, +20% Shield Regen, and +10% Hyperspace Cooldown natively to all player ships.\n'%_t, '')
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c2', 'ca_cat_a12', 'Automating Defense'%_t, 'Ascendant Gateways can be constructed to establish automated defense perimeters.\n- Function: When an allied station falls under attack, an Ascendant Gateway can instantly warp in a friendly response fleet using Ascendant Energy reserves.\n'%_t, '')

    -- Synergies & Integrations
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addChapter', 'ca_cat', 'ca_cat_c3', 'Synergies & Integrations'%_t)
    Player():invokeFunction('ui/cosmiccodex', 'addArticle', 'ca_cat_c3', 'ca_cat_a13', 'Cosmic Vault Synergy'%_t, 'Ascendancy utilizes several shared APIs provided by Cosmic Vault:\n- Eclipse Contraband: Illegal Ascendant tech can be fenced in Vault smuggling rings.\n- Dead Empire Filter: Vault Faction Index API tracks fallen empires and assigns them Eclipse Citadel conquer priority.\n- Relentless Expansion: Vault Territory API expands Eclipse borders naturally across the map.\n- Rift Spillage: Corrupted nodes spawn strange anomalies (via Vault Anomalies API).\n- Hazard Immunity: Eclipse ships utilize the Vault Buff API for weather immunities.\n- Post-Boss Anomalies: The destruction of a Citadel spawns exotic Vault-tracked anomalies for players to research.\n'%_t, '')
end
